<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chakradhar Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chakradhar Singh was the Raja of Raigarh, a princely state in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, from 1924. A musician and dancer himself, he gathered leading Kathak dancers, singers and instrumentalists at his court and compiled treatises on dance and rhythm, giving rise to the Raigarh gharana of Kathak. The annual Chakradhar Samaroh festival of music and dance in Raigarh commemorates him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chakradhar-singh.jpg" alt="Chakradhar Singh" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Monuraj124 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raja_Bahadur_Chakradhar_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
